==Strategy==
Bloodvelds are among the few monsters that use [[Magical melee|magic-based melee]] attacks. Although their attacks are classified as [[melee]], the player's [[magic defence]]—not melee [[defence]]—determines the accuracy of bloodveld attacks. Therefore, it is recommended when killing bloodvelds to equip armour with strong magic defence, such as [[dragonhide]], as bloodvelds are relatively accurate. Players using [[Prayer]] should use [[pray melee|Protect from Melee]] to nullify damage.

In the [[Slayer Tower]], bloodvelds can be [[safespotted]] in the centre room either in the north-eastern corner behind the chair or next to the armour stands and wardrobes around the walls. On the task-only basement floor, a safespot exists in the north-west corner between the chest, chair, broken table, and shelves. Bringing [[nature rune]]s for [[alchemy spells]] is recommended, as bloodvelds frequently drop [[fire rune]]s and items with good high alchemy value. An additional safespot is found in the corner between the torch and the armour set. 

In the [[Stronghold Slayer Cave]], bloodvelds can be safespotted while using a [[dwarf multicannon]] in the north-east section of their area, though this spot is often crowded. An additional safespot in the Stronghold Slayer Cave is located in the east room, north of some rocks and east of a pillar. 

In the [[God Wars Dungeon]], bloodvelds can be safespotted behind piles of bricks directly north-east of the exit rope, though a player should equip both a [[Saradomin item|Saradomin]] and [[Zamorak item]] when using this safespot. Another option exists further to the north-east, behind the rock formations on the coast. Once inside, this spot requires only a Zamorak item.

In the [[Wilderness God Wars Dungeon]], with both a [[Saradomin item|Saradomin]] and [[Zamorak item]] equipped, rocks can be used to safespot bloodvelds.

